{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q014_paper_example_reclassification_pa1492","answer":"In SCOP 1.69, PA1492 from PDB 1t1j was classified as domain d1t1ja_ with SCCS c.137.1.1: class c, its own fold c.137 "Hypothetical protein PA1492", its own superfamily c.137.1, and family c.137.1.1. Nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase from PDB 1f8y was domain d1f8ya_ with SCCS c.23.14.1: class c, fold c.23 "Flavodoxin-like", superfamily c.23.14 "N-deoxyribosyltransferase", and family c.23.14.1. Thus, in 1.69 these two classified domains shared only class c, alpha/beta proteins; SCOP made no fold-level or superfamily-level relationship between PA1492 and 1f8y.

In the current SCOPe release returned by the service, 2.08, the same PA1492 public domain SUNID 106249 is d1t1ja1 with boundary 1t1j A:1-118, and its family "Hypothetical protein PA1492" has moved to c.23.14.2 under the Flavodoxin-like fold c.23 and the N-(deoxy)ribosyltransferase-like superfamily c.23.14. 1f8y chain A remains d1f8ya_ in the neighboring N-deoxyribosyltransferase family c.23.14.1. The relationship therefore changed from SCOP-1.69 "same class only" to current SCOPe "same superfamily but different families": PA1492 and nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase are now placed in distinct families inside a shared homology-bearing superfamily, so SCOPe supports probable common ancestry rather than merely a broad alpha/beta-class resemblance.

The current placement does not make PA1492 a member of the N-deoxyribosyltransferase family c.23.14.1, and it does not by itself transfer the exact nucleoside 2-deoxyribosyltransferase activity, substrate specificity, ligand-bound state, oligomeric behavior, or whole-protein function of 1f8y to PA1492. The retrieved SCOPe superfamily record notes similar active-site architectures and catalytic mechanisms among functionally characterized members, but the SCOPe responses establish the before/after classification, not the Andreeva et al. 2008 structural alignment, sequence evidence, or curator rationale for the reclassification; those stronger mechanistic details would need paper, alignment, active-site, and biochemical evidence outside the hierarchy.","evidence_used":["skill: scop-homology/SKILL.md","skill: scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","skill: scop-homology/references/biological-interpretation.md","MCP tool: resolve_scop_identifier","MCP tool: get_scop_domains","MCP tool: get_scop_node","MCP tool: compare_scop_domains","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/resolve/1t1j","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/resolve/1f8y","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/resolve/d1t1ja_","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/resolve/d1f8ya_","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1t1ja_","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1t1ja_/parents","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1t1ja_/annotations","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1t1ja_/homology","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_/parents","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_/annotations","REST: /api/v1/releases/1.69/sids/d1f8ya_/homology","REST: /api/v1/releases/current","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/1t1j","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/resolve/1f8y","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sunids/106249","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1/parents","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1/annotations","REST: /api/v1/releases/2.08/sids/d1t1ja1/homology","REST: /api/v